[49m[38;5;10m+     1[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # CONFIGS.md — configuration surface table (Phase A, gate for Phase B)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Derived mechanically from `c_src/src/lib.c` + `c_src/include/lib.h`. The axes the C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m code actually branches on / dispatches on:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis O — operation selection.** `operation_func` dispatch is the library's only
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m runtime "mode". It is set three ways: `get_operation(opcode)` with `opcode ∈ 0..3`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (L67–81), or a function pointer handed directly to `execute_operation` (L83) /
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `apply_operation` (L128). The four modes are `multiply_with_static`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `add_with_static`, `xor_operation`, `shift_with_static`, plus the NULL mode
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (see `ERRORS.md`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis S — static tuning state** (L45–47): `static_multiplier = 3`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `static_addend = 100`, `static_shift_amount = 2`. Internal linkage, never written,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m so these are fixed constants that each op path must bake in identically.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis V — integer value shape.** Every op is `int`-in/`int`-out with wrapping
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m signed arithmetic (`*`, `+`), bitwise xor against `0xABCD`, a signed **left** shift
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m that discards high bits, and a signed **arithmetic right** shift. So the distinct
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m value shapes are: zero, ±1, small ±, high-bit-set (left-shift discard), negative
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (arithmetic-shift sign fill), `INT_MAX`/`INT_MIN` (overflow), and `0xABCD` /
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `0xFFFF` / `0xDEADBEEF`-related constants.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis C — element count / buffer shape** for `compute_checksum` (L97–114):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `count ∈ {1,2,3,4}` (byte loop length `4*count`), plus the `> 4` clamp. The byte
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m loop reinterprets `int*` as `unsigned char*`, so **host byte order** is part of the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m observable contract.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis T — carried struct state** for `ComputeState` (L38–42): `accumulator`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `operation_count` (incremented only on a successful `apply_operation`), `checksum`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Distinct shapes: fresh / one op applied / many ops applied / re-initialised.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis X — caller/callee library crossing.** Both `.so`s export *both* the leaf ops
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and the higher-order consumers, so a real consumer can mix them: a C function
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m pointer into Rust's `execute_operation`/`apply_operation` and vice versa, and a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `ComputeState` buffer mutated alternately by both libraries.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis F — Cargo features.** `translation/Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m table, so there is exactly one build configuration (default ≡
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `--no-default-features`). Asserted by `tests/symbols.rs::no_cargo_features_declared`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every row is exercised with many randomized inputs (fixed seed, SplitMix64 —
